<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>PHP YARA Vulnerability Scanner v4 – CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (Windows)</Title>
    <Description>&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;
.phpScan {font-family:Segoe UI,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#243447;max-width:1000px;margin:8px 12px 20px;}
.phpScan h2 {font-size:20px;color:#183953;margin:0 0 5px;}
.phpScan h3 {font-size:15px;color:#183953;margin:20px 0 8px;padding-bottom:5px;border-bottom:2px solid #dbe5ed;}
.phpScan p {margin:7px 0;}
.phpScan .recommend {background:#edf5fa;border-left:4px solid #28658a;padding:10px 12px;margin:12px 0;}
.phpScan table {width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed;margin:8px 0;}
.phpScan th {background:#edf1f5;text-align:left;font-weight:600;}
.phpScan td,.phpScan th {padding:8px;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #dce3e9;word-wrap:break-word;}
.phpScan .setting {width:31%;}.phpScan .value {width:18%;}
.phpScan .mode {width:110px;}.phpScan .deep {background:#fff7e7;}
.phpScan .warning {color:#865000;font-weight:bold;}
.phpScan input,.phpScan select,.phpScan button {font-family:inherit;font-size:13px;}
.phpScan input {max-width:95%;}.phpScan input[type=text],.phpScan input:not([type]) {box-sizing:border-box;padding:5px;border:1px solid #9baab7;}
.phpScan select {padding:5px;max-width:100%;}.phpScan input[type=checkbox] {margin-top:3px;}
.phpScan .exclusion input {display:block;width:98%;margin:5px 0;}
.phpScan .hint {color:#516170;font-size:12px;}
.phpScan code {font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;word-wrap:break-word;}
.phpScan .launch {border-top:1px solid #dce3e9;padding-top:12px;margin-top:15px;}
.phpScan button {background:#245b7d;color:white;border:1px solid #194766;padding:8px 16px;cursor:pointer;}
.phpScan button:focus,.phpScan input:focus,.phpScan select:focus {outline:2px solid #438bb7;outline-offset:1px;}
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;div class="phpScan"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;PHP vulnerability scan&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Find PHP runtime versions affected by &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109618&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;CVE-2026-109619&lt;/strong&gt; on Windows, without running PHP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Version compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Use the v4 scanners with the v4 Results Analysis. Scanner and Analysis versions should match. Run a new scan after upgrading to refresh the results.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="recommend"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended: start with Quick Scan and leave the limits at their defaults.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Choose a broader scan only when needed. More coverage increases disk activity and run time.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Document, media, font, ordinary text, source, archive, package, debug and selected asset file types are skipped in every scan type, including Deep. Native executables and libraries remain eligible; php-config and php_version.h are retained when PHP build-text detection is enabled. A runtime renamed with an excluded extension, such as .js or .zip, can be missed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;1. Choose a scan type&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;label for="PHPScanPreset"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scan type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/label&gt; &lt;select id="PHPScanPreset" onchange="PhpScan.preset(this.value);"&gt;&lt;option value="quick" selected="selected"&gt;QUICK SCAN (recommended)&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="normal"&gt;NORMAL SCAN&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="deep"&gt;DEEP SCAN&lt;/option&gt;&lt;option value="custom" disabled="disabled"&gt;CUSTOM (advanced settings)&lt;/option&gt;&lt;/select&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="mode" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Scan&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Coverage and tradeoff&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quick&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Standard PHP runtime names in the usual application locations. Fastest; can miss renamed or embedded runtimes.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 10 min search; 10 min content scan; 5 million files; 30 GiB candidate input; 512 MiB per file; 10% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Normal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Also checks renamed/nonstandard binaries, while keeping the usual folder exclusions. Broader runtime coverage; takes longer.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 30 min search; 30 min content scan; 10 million files; 40 GiB candidate input; 512 MiB per file; 10% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr class="deep"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Also includes normally skipped OS/cache/data locations and PHP build text. &lt;span class="warning"&gt;WARNING: This takes much longer and is more likely to hit file and scan limits. Deep already uses the maximum search time, content scan time, file count and total candidate input; it can still hit limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="hint"&gt;Limits: 60 min search; 60 min content scan; 10 million files; 100 GiB candidate input; 1 GiB per file; 25% YARA CPU.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Choosing a scan type fills its recommended limits below. Quick and Normal use 512 MiB per file and 10% YARA CPU. Deep uses 1 GiB per file and 25% YARA CPU, with the maximum allowed time, file-count and candidate-input budgets. You can adjust individual settings afterward. Remote storage, cloud placeholders and other permanent exclusions still apply. Build text alone does not prove an installed vulnerable runtime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;2. Advanced settings (optional)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Changing coverage or a preset limit updates the scan type above; a non-preset combination is shown as Custom. Choosing another scan type resets these settings to its recommended values. Additional directory exclusions and extra-gentle disk access are retained.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="setting" /&gt;&lt;col class="value" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"&gt;Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Scans other native binary names; leaving this off can miss renamed or custom embedded PHP.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"&gt;Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Restores OS, recovery, cache and data locations normally excluded, while retaining scan limits.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBuildText"&gt;Include PHP source/build text (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBuildText"   onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Includes PHP build/header evidence without treating it as an installed runtime.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Time and resource limits&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="setting" /&gt;&lt;col class="value" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPEnumerationSeconds"&gt;File search time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPEnumerationSeconds" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Stops searching after this many minutes and marks unfinished coverage as partial. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPScanSeconds"&gt;Content scan time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPScanSeconds" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Limits YARA content scanning to this many minutes and reports partial results if it times out. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFiles"&gt;Maximum files checked&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFiles" value="5000000" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps files considered during discovery to bound work on unusually large filesystems. (Allowed: 1000 to 10000000.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCandidateGB"&gt;Maximum candidate input (GiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCandidateGB" value="30" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps the combined size of files sent to YARA; exceeding this reports a partial scan. (Allowed: 1 to 100.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFileMB"&gt;Maximum individual file size (MiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFileMB" value="512" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Skips individual files at or above this size; 512 MiB covers normal PHP and large embedded builds. (Allowed: 16 to 2048.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCpuLimit"&gt;YARA CPU setting (%)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCpuLimit" value="10" size="12"  onchange="PhpScan.syncPreset();" onkeyup="PhpScan.syncPreset();" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Sets the YARA engine CPU target; this is not a total system CPU guarantee. (Allowed: 1 to 50.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPGentleDisk"&gt;Extra-gentle disk access (slower, Windows only)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPGentleDisk"  /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Uses lower disk scheduling priority to reduce disk contention, which can slow the scan.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Additional directory exclusions (optional)&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class="exclusion"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;label for="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"&gt;Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;input id="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" value="" size="48" maxlength="4096" /&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Skip your chosen folders; leave blank for no additional exclusions. See the examples below.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope="col"&gt;What is skipped&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/data/*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;C:\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The named directory and all its subdirectories.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/data/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;C:\folder\&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Only files directly in that directory; subdirectories are still searched.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;*/data/*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;code&gt;*\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Every matching directory and its subdirectories, wherever found.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Separate entries with commas, without quotes. Use an absolute path or a leading */; * includes path separators and other characters are literal. Windows ignores case; Linux/macOS matching is case-sensitive. Spaces are supported; commas inside a folder name are not. Maximum 32 entries and 4096 UTF-8 bytes. Exclusions apply to every scan type, can hide PHP, and are logged; intentional exclusions do not mark a scan partial.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="launch"&gt;&lt;button onclick="return PhpScan.prepare();"&gt;Configure and Take Action&lt;/button&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Opens the standard Console Take Action dialog, where you select computers. These settings apply only to that action. API/WebUI actions without parameters use Quick defaults; API integrations can supply the same parameters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Reading the results&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;colgroup&gt;&lt;col class="mode" /&gt;&lt;col /&gt;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;An upstream-affected PHP runtime was found. Check vendor patch status and web exposure before deciding remediation.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FALSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;No affected runtime was found within the completed, selected scan scope.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UNKNOWN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;A short reason identifies unavailable results, incomplete coverage or evidence that needs verification. Vendor backports require checking the package advisory.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;Positive findings are retained during a partial scan. BigFix action status Fixed confirms that the background scan started, not that it finished. Use the matching Results Analysis to check scan progress and final results. While a scan runs or after an interruption, the properties explain that state; the previous completed summary stays on disk until replaced by a new usable result.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Coverage and requirements&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quick checks php, php-cgi, php-fpm, phpdbg, lsphp, frankenphp, libphp and mod_php name families, including version suffixes and native runtime libraries (.exe/.dll on Windows, .so/.so.N on Linux, .dylib/.so on macOS). PHP core DLLs and server modules are included. Ordinary .php application scripts do not identify an installed runtime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Legitimate per-user applications remain in scope, including common PHP installations such as Herd, Scoop, Homebrew, MAMP and XAMPP where applicable. OS/recovery trees, caches, backups and personal data are skipped unless broader locations are selected. Network storage, cloud-only files, symlinks, snapshots and scanner/cache data remain excluded. Archives and container images are not unpacked. Meaningful access restrictions and limits produce partial coverage; the scanner does not change system access or privacy settings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Windows 10/11 x64 and Windows Server 2016 or later, with Windows PowerShell 5.1/.NET.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Minimum ActionScript syntax: BigFix Client 9.5.7. Use a client supported on the target OS and architecture; this syntax minimum does not establish ARM64 support. The pinned YARA-X engine is delivered by BigFix. No endpoint Python, PHP or compiler is required.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Detailed scan log&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;code&gt;YARA_PHP/scan.log&lt;/code&gt; under the BigFix client state root:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\YARA_PHP\scan.log&lt;/code&gt; (typical Windows location)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;summary.txt supplies the four Analysis properties; scan.lock prevents overlapping scans. Temporary action work is removed after completion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="hint"&gt;Community utility, not HCL-supported patch content. Rule source: &lt;a href="https://github.com/bigfix/Site_Rapid_Response"&gt;Site Rapid Response&lt;/a&gt; (Apache-2.0).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;var phpScanFields = [{"key": "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex", "label": "Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)", "text": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames", "label": "Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations", "label": "Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBuildText", "label": "Include PHP source/build text (slower)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}, {"key": "PHPEnumerationSeconds", "label": "File search time (minutes)", "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60}, {"key": "PHPScanSeconds", "label": "Content scan time (minutes)", "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60}, {"key": "PHPMaxFiles", "label": "Maximum files checked", "min": 1000, "max": 10000000}, {"key": "PHPCandidateGB", "label": "Maximum candidate input (GiB)", "min": 1, "max": 100}, {"key": "PHPMaxFileMB", "label": "Maximum individual file size (MiB)", "min": 16, "max": 2048}, {"key": "PHPCpuLimit", "label": "YARA CPU setting (%)", "min": 1, "max": 50}, {"key": "PHPGentleDisk", "label": "Extra-gentle disk access (slower, Windows only)", "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true}];
var phpScanWindows = true;
/* Console JScript compatible: no JSON dependency, eval, credentials or target selection. */
var PhpScan = (function () {
    function parameters(values) {
        var fields = phpScanFields, selected = {}, index, field, text, number, multiplier, minimum, maximum;
        for (index = 0; index &lt; fields.length; index++) {
            field = fields[index];
            text = String(values[field.key]);
            if (field.text) {
                // Encode UTF-8 bytes, never interpolate a directory into script code.
                if (/[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/.test(text)) { throw new Error('Exclusions cannot contain control characters.'); }
                var entries = text.split(','), clean = [], j, entry, encoded, hex = 'x', k, byte;
                for (j = 0; j &lt; entries.length; j++) {
                    entry = entries[j].replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '');
                    if (!entry) { continue; }
                    var prefix = phpScanWindows ? /^([A-Za-z]:[\\\/]|\*[\\\/])/ : /^(\/|\*\/)/;
                    var relative = phpScanWindows ? /(^|[\\\/])\.{1,2}([\\\/]|$)/ : /(^|\/)\.{1,2}(\/|$)/;
                    if (!prefix.test(entry) || relative.test(entry)) {
                        throw new Error('Use absolute exclusion paths or a leading */; . and .. segments are not allowed.');
                    }
                    clean.push(entry);
                }
                if (clean.length &gt; 32) { throw new Error('Use at most 32 directory exclusions.'); }
                encoded = encodeURIComponent(clean.join(','));
                for (k = 0; k &lt; encoded.length; k++) {
                    if (encoded.charAt(k) === '%') { byte = encoded.substr(k + 1, 2); k += 2; }
                    else { byte = encoded.charCodeAt(k).toString(16); if (byte.length &lt; 2) { byte = '0' + byte; } }
                    hex += byte.toLowerCase();
                }
                if (hex.length &gt; 8193) { throw new Error('Directory exclusions must fit within 4096 UTF-8 bytes.'); }
                selected[field.key] = hex;
                continue;
            }
            if (!/^[0-9]{1,9}$/.test(text)) { throw new Error(field.label + ': enter a whole number.'); }
            number = Number(text);
            multiplier = field.multiplier || 1;
            minimum = Math.ceil(field.min / multiplier);
            maximum = Math.floor(field.max / multiplier);
            if (number &lt; minimum || number &gt; maximum) { throw new Error(field.label + ': use ' + minimum + ' to ' + maximum + '.'); }
            number = number * multiplier;
            selected[field.key] = String(number);
        }
        return selected;
    }
    function prepare() {
        try {
            var values = {}, index, field;
            for (index = 0; index &lt; phpScanFields.length; index++) {
                field = phpScanFields[index];
                values[field.key] = field.checkbox ? (document.getElementById(field.key).checked ? '1' : '0') : document.getElementById(field.key).value;
            }
            var selected = parameters(values);
            if (typeof TakeFixletAction === 'undefined' || typeof Relevance === 'undefined') {
                throw new Error('Open this content in the BigFix Console to use this settings form. API/WebUI launches use defaults unless action parameters are supplied.');
            }
            // These are ordinary, nonsecret action parameters. The Console
            // obtains the current Task's Action1; no XML or script is rebuilt.
            TakeFixletAction(Relevance('id of current fixlet'), Relevance('id of current bes site'), 'Action1', selected);
        } catch (error) { alert('Cannot prepare scan. ' + error.message); }
        return false;
    }
    var presetFields = ["PHPEnumerationSeconds", "PHPScanSeconds", "PHPMaxFiles", "PHPCandidateGB", "PHPMaxFileMB", "PHPCpuLimit", "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames", "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations", "PHPIncludeBuildText"];
    var presetValues = {"quick": [10, 10, 5000000, 30, 512, 10, false, false, false], "normal": [30, 30, 10000000, 40, 512, 10, true, false, false], "deep": [60, 60, 10000000, 100, 1024, 25, true, true, true]};
    function preset(value) {
        var values = presetValues[value], i, field;
        if (!values) { return; }
        for (i = 0; i &lt; presetFields.length; i++) {
            field = document.getElementById(presetFields[i]);
            if (i &lt; 6) { field.value = String(values[i]); }
            else { field.checked = values[i]; }
        }
        document.getElementById('PHPScanPreset').value = value;
    }
    function syncPreset() {
        var modes = ['quick','normal','deep'], mode, values, i, matches, selected = 'custom', field;
        for (mode = 0; mode &lt; modes.length; mode++) {
            values = presetValues[modes[mode]];
            matches = true;
            for (i = 0; i &lt; presetFields.length; i++) {
                field = document.getElementById(presetFields[i]);
                if (i &lt; 6 ? String(field.value) !== String(values[i]) : field.checked !== values[i]) {
                    matches = false;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (matches) { selected = modes[mode]; break; }
        }
        document.getElementById('PHPScanPreset').value = selected;
    }
    return {parameters: parameters, prepare: prepare, preset: preset, syncPreset: syncPreset};
}());
document.body.ontakeaction = function () { return PhpScan.prepare(); };
&lt;/script&gt;&lt;p&gt;API-only PHP extension markers are logged as supporting evidence; they do not by themselves make a scan UNKNOWN.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background scanning:&lt;/strong&gt; The BigFix action waits only for the scan to start, then other actions can run. Fixed means the scan launched; check the Results Analysis for Running, completed or interrupted status. Only one PHP scan runs at a time. Completed results and scan.log stay in YARA_PHP; temporary scan files are removed after the worker stops. Stopping the launch action after it finishes does not cancel the background scan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</Description>
    <Relevance>if (version of client &gt;= "9.5.7") then (if windows of operating system then (x64 of operating system and (exists (it as string as version) whose (it &gt;= "5.1" as version) of values "PowerShellVersion" of keys "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\PowerShell\3\PowerShellEngine" of native registry) and (if product type of operating system = nt workstation product type then version of operating system &gt;= "10.0.10240" as version else if product type of operating system = nt server product type or product type of operating system = nt domain controller product type then version of operating system &gt;= "10.0.14393" as version else false)) else false) else false</Relevance>
    <Category>PHP Security Discovery</Category>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to run bounded local PHP discovery.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">begin prefetch block
add prefetch item name=yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip sha1=344da50ce1693edd32b92c7d32eaf26d99c97f17 sha256=eac36a58699b94d3732a7fe1d8453fe89e0077bb18ac2c99b4c2ee102a431f2e size=9081400 url=https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/download/v1.22.0/yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip
end prefetch block
action uses file encoding UTF-8 NoBOM
action uses wow64 redirection false
if {not exists parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"}
parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = "x"
endif
continue if {length of parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" &lt;= 8193 and parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = regex "x([0-9A-Fa-f][0-9A-Fa-f])*"}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"}
parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds"}
parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = "600"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPScanSeconds"}
parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = "600"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPScanSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFiles"}
parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = "5000000"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFiles" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &gt;= 1000 and (parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &lt;= 10000000}
if {not exists parameter "PHPCandidateGB"}
parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = "30"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPCandidateGB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &gt;= 1 and (parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &lt;= 100}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFileMB"}
parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = "512"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &gt;= 16 and (parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &lt;= 2048}
